<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9843" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concīsĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		2. concido, prop., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cutting;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a cutting to pieces,
				destruction</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Joel, 3,
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A mutilation</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Phil. 3,
				2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			In rhet., <i>a separating of a sentence into short
				divisions</i> or <i>clauses</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Part.
				Or. 6, 19</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
